WEBVTT

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:07.541
Previously on Supernatural

00:00:07.576 --> 00:00:08.221
Dad?

00:00:08.256 --> 00:00:10.316
Sam. This is bigger than you
think. They're everywhere.

00:00:10.351 --> 00:00:12.404
He wants us to pick
up where he left off.

00:00:12.439 --> 00:00:14.668
Saving people. Hunting things.

00:00:14.703 --> 00:00:16.175
The family business.

00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:17.648
I got to find dad.

00:00:18.355 --> 00:00:20.578
I dreamt about Jessica's
death before it happened.

00:00:20.613 --> 00:00:21.543
You got to be careful, all right?

00:00:21.578 --> 00:00:24.164
Ghosts are attracted to that
whole ESP thing you got going.

00:00:24.199 --> 00:00:26.580
I told you I don't have ESP.
I just have strange vibes.

00:00:26.615 --> 00:00:29.801
Weird dreams. Dead people
have weird dreams, man.

00:00:29.836 --> 00:00:32.987
I have these nightmares.
Sometimes they come true.

00:00:33.291 --> 00:00:34.587
Come again?

00:02:03.346 --> 00:02:05.736
Somebody help me! Somebody...!

00:02:06.383 --> 00:02:08.177
Somebody help...!

00:02:38.666 --> 00:02:39.683
Dean.

00:02:40.942 --> 00:02:42.211
Dean.

00:02:44.877 --> 00:02:47.438
What are you doing, man? It's
in the middle of the night.

00:02:47.656 --> 00:02:49.428
We have to go.

00:02:49.603 --> 00:02:51.685
What's happening? We have to go.

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:53.218
Right now.

00:02:57.913 --> 00:02:58.795
Mcreedy.

00:02:58.830 --> 00:03:01.205
Detective Mcreedy. Badge number 158.

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:03.621
I've got a signal four
eighty on progress.

00:03:03.656 --> 00:03:07.124
I need a registered
owner of a Two door Sedan.

00:03:07.159 --> 00:03:10.592
Michigan license plate
Mary, Frank, 6-0-3-7.

00:03:10.627 --> 00:03:12.069
Yeah, okay. Just hurry.

00:03:12.104 --> 00:03:13.473
Sammy, relax.

00:03:13.508 --> 00:03:16.758
I'm sure, its just a nightmare.
Yeah. Tell me about it.

00:03:16.793 --> 00:03:20.008
I mean it. You know, a normal
everyday naked class nightmare.

00:03:20.043 --> 00:03:22.359
This license plate, it
won't check out. You'll see.

00:03:22.394 --> 00:03:24.270
It felt different Dean. Real.

00:03:24.305 --> 00:03:26.726
Like we dreamt about our
old house and Jessica.

00:03:26.761 --> 00:03:29.612
Oh, yeah. That makes sense. Dreaming
about our house, your girlfriend.

00:03:29.647 --> 00:03:31.471
This guy in your dream,
you ever seen him before?

00:03:31.506 --> 00:03:33.003
No... No, exactly.

00:03:33.038 --> 00:03:35.687
Why would you have premonitions
about some random dude in Michigan?

00:03:35.722 --> 00:03:37.044
I don't know. Yeah, me neither.

00:03:37.079 --> 00:03:38.475
Yes, I'm here.

00:03:42.143 --> 00:03:44.718
Jim Miller, Saginaw Michigan.

00:03:44.753 --> 00:03:47.294
You have the street address?

00:03:48.095 --> 00:03:50.450
Got it. Thanks.

00:03:52.510 --> 00:03:54.139
It checks out.

00:03:54.174 --> 00:03:55.768
How far are we?

00:03:56.759 --> 00:03:58.086
From Saginaw? Yeah.

00:03:58.121 --> 00:03:59.799
A couple of hours.

00:04:01.507 --> 00:04:03.403
Drive faster.

00:04:54.171 --> 00:04:55.659
What happened?

00:04:55.694 --> 00:04:57.645
Suicide.

00:04:58.309 --> 00:05:01.022
I can't believe it.

00:05:02.977 --> 00:05:04.591
Did you know him?

00:05:04.626 --> 00:05:08.390
Saw him everyday at Saint Augustine.

00:05:08.425 --> 00:05:12.155
Always seems... seemed so normal.

00:05:12.331 --> 00:05:15.413
I guess you never know what's
going behind closed doors.

00:05:15.448 --> 00:05:18.107
I guess not. How did uh...

00:05:18.142 --> 00:05:20.732
What are they saying happened?

00:05:20.767 --> 00:05:22.812
I heard they found him in the garage

00:05:22.847 --> 00:05:26.463
Locked inside his car
with the engine running.

00:05:27.327 --> 00:05:29.444
Do you know about what
time they found him?

00:05:29.479 --> 00:05:32.158
It just happened an hour or two ago.

00:05:32.193 --> 00:05:34.141
His poor family.

00:05:34.176 --> 00:05:37.950
I can't even imagine what
they're going through.

00:05:56.221 --> 00:05:57.829
Sam, we got here as fast as we could.

00:05:57.864 --> 00:05:59.955
Not fast enough.

00:06:00.585 --> 00:06:03.106
Which doesn't make any sense, man.

00:06:03.141 --> 00:06:05.157
Why would I even have these premonitions

00:06:05.192 --> 00:06:07.597
Unless there was a chance that
I can stop them from happening.

00:06:07.632 --> 00:06:09.298
I don't know.

00:06:14.637 --> 00:06:17.174
So, what do you think killed him?

00:06:17.376 --> 00:06:19.081
Maybe the guy killed himself.

00:06:19.116 --> 00:06:22.109
Maybe there's nothing
supernatural going on at all.

00:06:22.144 --> 00:06:24.824
I'm telling you. I watched it happen.

00:06:24.859 --> 00:06:27.504
He was murdered by something Dean.

00:06:27.539 --> 00:06:29.559
It trapped him in the garage.

00:06:29.594 --> 00:06:31.364
Like what? A spirit?
A poltergeist? What?

00:06:31.399 --> 00:06:32.856
I don't know what it was.

00:06:32.891 --> 00:06:35.085
I don't know why I'm
having these dreams.

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:37.280
I don't know what the
hell is happening Dean.

00:06:37.555 --> 00:06:39.141
What?

00:06:39.176 --> 00:06:41.761
Nothing, man. I'm
just worried about you.

00:06:41.796 --> 00:06:43.867
Well, don't look at me like that.

00:06:43.902 --> 00:06:45.939
I'm not looking at you like anything.

00:06:46.163 --> 00:06:48.436
But I got to say. You look like crap.

00:06:48.471 --> 00:06:51.380
Nice, thanks. You welcome.

00:06:51.563 --> 00:06:54.355
Come on, let's just pick
this up in the morning.

00:06:54.390 --> 00:06:57.147
Check out the house,
we'll talk to the family.

00:06:57.607 --> 00:07:00.351
Dean, you saw them. They're devastated.

00:07:00.386 --> 00:07:03.095
They're not gonna want to talk to us.

00:07:04.517 --> 00:07:06.675
Yeah, you're right.

00:07:07.444 --> 00:07:10.005
But I think I know who they'll talk to.

00:07:11.079 --> 00:07:12.969
Who?

00:07:16.805 --> 00:07:19.770
This has got to be a
whole new loaf for us.

00:07:24.258 --> 00:07:25.940
Good afternoon.

00:07:25.975 --> 00:07:28.560
I'm Father Simmons.
This is Father Freely.

00:07:28.595 --> 00:07:31.146
We're new junior priests
at Saint Augustine.

00:07:31.181 --> 00:07:32.989
May we come in?

00:07:34.137 --> 00:07:35.556
Thanks.

00:07:36.153 --> 00:07:38.143
We're very sorry for your loss.

00:07:40.046 --> 00:07:43.800
In difficult times like these when the
Lord's guidance is most needed. Look...

00:07:43.835 --> 00:07:46.349
You want to pitch your whole
Lord has a plan thing fine.

00:07:46.384 --> 00:07:48.800
Don't pitch it to me. My brother's dead.

00:07:48.835 --> 00:07:51.386
Roger, please.

00:07:52.869 --> 00:07:54.813
Excuse me.

00:07:57.364 --> 00:08:00.529
I'm sorry about my brother in law.

00:08:00.564 --> 00:08:03.695
He's just so upset about Jim's death.

00:08:03.730 --> 00:08:05.375
Would you like some coffee?

00:08:05.410 --> 00:08:07.083
That'll be great.

00:08:10.136 --> 00:08:13.138
It was wonderful of you to stop by.

00:08:13.173 --> 00:08:15.846
The support of the church
means so much right now.

00:08:15.881 --> 00:08:17.049
Of course.

00:08:17.084 --> 00:08:20.302
After all, we all are god's children.

00:08:27.789 --> 00:08:28.912
What?

00:08:28.947 --> 00:08:33.019
Just tone it down a little bit, Father.

00:08:38.013 --> 00:08:39.649
So, Ms. Miller.

00:08:39.684 --> 00:08:42.684
Did your husband have
a history of depression?

00:08:42.719 --> 00:08:44.501
Nothing like that.

00:08:44.536 --> 00:08:48.608
We... had our ups and
downs like everyone.

00:08:48.643 --> 00:08:51.054
But we were happy.

00:08:52.450 --> 00:08:55.234
I just don't understand

00:08:55.269 --> 00:08:58.740
How Jim could do something like that.

00:09:00.775 --> 00:09:04.424
I'm so sorry you had
to find him like that.

00:09:04.586 --> 00:09:06.814
Actually...

00:09:06.849 --> 00:09:09.042
Our son, Max.

00:09:09.519 --> 00:09:12.523
He was the one who found him.

00:09:12.558 --> 00:09:15.335
Do you mind if maybe...
I go talk to him?

00:09:15.370 --> 00:09:16.529
No.

00:09:16.564 --> 00:09:18.773
Oh, thank you Father.

00:09:30.765 --> 00:09:32.078
Max?

00:09:32.113 --> 00:09:34.015
Hey, I'm Sam.

00:09:37.734 --> 00:09:40.691
Ms. Miller, you have a lovely home.

00:09:41.181 --> 00:09:44.226
How long have you lived here?

00:09:44.261 --> 00:09:47.271
We moved in about five years ago.

00:09:48.115 --> 00:09:50.942
You know, the only problem
with these old houses

00:09:50.977 --> 00:09:54.163
I bet you have all kinds of headaches.

00:09:54.198 --> 00:09:56.164
Like what?

00:09:56.199 --> 00:09:58.095
Well...

00:09:58.130 --> 00:10:00.653
Weird leaks.

00:10:00.688 --> 00:10:02.827
Electrical shortages.

00:10:02.862 --> 00:10:06.789
Odd sort of noises at
night. That kind of things.

00:10:08.136 --> 00:10:10.935
No, nothing like that.

00:10:11.105 --> 00:10:13.370
It's been perfect.

00:10:19.268 --> 00:10:20.657
May I use your restroom?

00:10:20.692 --> 00:10:23.310
Oh, sure. It's just up the stairs.

00:10:23.345 --> 00:10:24.829
Okay.

00:10:27.998 --> 00:10:30.515
So, what was your dad like?

00:10:31.593 --> 00:10:33.861
Just a normal dad.

00:10:33.896 --> 00:10:35.313
Yeah.

00:10:35.348 --> 00:10:38.573
You live at home now?

00:10:38.608 --> 00:10:40.186
Yeah.

00:10:40.221 --> 00:10:44.030
I'm trying to save up
for school but it's hard.

00:10:51.385 --> 00:10:54.795
So, when you found your dad?

00:10:55.730 --> 00:10:58.102
I woke up.

00:10:58.955 --> 00:11:01.782
I heard the engine running.

00:11:05.803 --> 00:11:08.744
I don't know why he did it.

00:11:12.088 --> 00:11:14.186
I know its ruff.

00:11:14.221 --> 00:11:16.250
Losing a parent.

00:11:16.285 --> 00:11:20.087
Especially when you don't
have all the answers.

00:12:15.159 --> 00:12:16.755
Anything?

00:12:16.790 --> 00:12:18.395
Zip.

00:12:21.499 --> 00:12:24.083
Escanaba Motel No Vacancy

00:12:26.926 --> 00:12:29.238
So, what do you have? Well, nothing.

00:12:29.273 --> 00:12:32.101
Nothing bad has happened to the
Miller house since it was built.

00:12:32.136 --> 00:12:34.213
What about the land? No
graveyard, battlefields,

00:12:34.248 --> 00:12:39.286
Tribal lands or any other kind of
atrocity on or near the property.

00:12:40.017 --> 00:12:42.043
Hey, man. I told you. I
searched the house up and down.

00:12:42.078 --> 00:12:45.879
There were no cold spots,
no soul person, nada.

00:12:46.366 --> 00:12:48.353
And the family said
everything was normal.

00:12:48.388 --> 00:12:50.306
Well, if there was a
demon or poltergeist.

00:12:50.341 --> 00:12:52.139
You don't think somebody
would have notice something?

00:12:52.174 --> 00:12:55.256
I used the infrared thermo
scanner, man. There was nothing.

00:12:55.291 --> 00:12:57.743
So what? You think Jim
Miller killed himself?

00:12:57.778 --> 00:13:02.585
And my dream was some sort
of freakish coincidence?

00:13:02.620 --> 00:13:04.154
I don't know.

00:13:04.690 --> 00:13:07.635
I'm pretty sure there's nothing
supernatural about that house.

00:13:07.670 --> 00:13:09.256
Yeah.

00:13:09.291 --> 00:13:10.842
Well...

00:13:11.517 --> 00:13:13.656
You know, maybe...

00:13:13.691 --> 00:13:15.970
Maybe there's nothing
to do with the house.

00:13:16.005 --> 00:13:18.217
Maybe it's just a...

00:13:18.252 --> 00:13:21.577
Gosh. Maybe it's connected to Jim.

00:13:21.612 --> 00:13:23.821
In some other way.

00:13:23.856 --> 00:13:26.031
What's wrong with you?

00:13:27.764 --> 00:13:29.140
My head!

00:13:29.175 --> 00:13:30.517
Sam?

00:13:32.145 --> 00:13:33.173
Hey!

00:13:33.399 --> 00:13:34.641
Hey!

00:13:34.810 --> 00:13:37.021
What's going on? Talk to me.

00:15:17.104 --> 00:15:18.620
It's happening again!

00:15:18.655 --> 00:15:20.964
Something's gonna kill Roger Miller.

00:15:26.242 --> 00:15:28.022
Roger Miller?

00:15:28.679 --> 00:15:31.578
No, no, just the address please.

00:15:32.949 --> 00:15:34.810
Okay, thanks.

00:15:36.121 --> 00:15:40.265
450 West Grove. Apartment 1120.

00:15:40.300 --> 00:15:42.074
You okay?

00:15:42.323 --> 00:15:45.841
Yeah. If you're goon hurl. I'll
pull the car over, you know.

00:15:45.876 --> 00:15:48.288
I'm fine. Just drive.

00:15:48.323 --> 00:15:49.951
All right.

00:15:52.943 --> 00:15:54.469
Dean, I'm scared man.

00:15:54.504 --> 00:15:56.168
These nightmares weren't bad enough.

00:15:56.203 --> 00:15:57.833
Now I'm seeing things when I'm awake?

00:15:57.868 --> 00:15:59.258
And theses...

00:15:59.293 --> 00:16:05.497
Visions or whatever. They're
getting intense, painful.

00:16:05.532 --> 00:16:07.016
Come on man. You'll be all right.

00:16:07.051 --> 00:16:10.198
You'll be fine. What
is it about the Millers?

00:16:10.233 --> 00:16:15.356
Why am I connected to them?
Why am I watching them die?

00:16:15.574 --> 00:16:17.884
Why the hell is this happening
to me? I don't know Sam.

00:16:17.919 --> 00:16:19.901
But we'll figure it out, okay?

00:16:19.936 --> 00:16:22.969
We face the unexplainable every
single day. This is just another thing.

00:16:23.004 --> 00:16:25.512
No. It's never been us.

00:16:25.547 --> 00:16:28.137
It's never been in the family like this.

00:16:28.172 --> 00:16:31.814
Tell the truth. You can't tell
me this doesn't freak you out.

00:16:34.549 --> 00:16:36.833
This doesn't freak me out.

00:16:45.981 --> 00:16:47.295
Hey, Roger!

00:16:47.330 --> 00:16:48.507
Hey, hold up a second.

00:16:48.542 --> 00:16:50.673
What are you guys,
missionaries? Leave me alone.

00:16:50.708 --> 00:16:52.227
Please!

00:16:57.800 --> 00:16:59.105
Hey! Roger!

00:16:59.140 --> 00:17:01.274
We're trying to help!
Please! Hey, hey, hey!

00:17:01.309 --> 00:17:03.026
Hey, hey, hey!

00:17:03.297 --> 00:17:05.062
I don't want your help.

00:17:05.097 --> 00:17:06.782
We're not priests. You've
got to listen to us!

00:17:06.817 --> 00:17:09.118
Roger, you're in danger!

00:17:10.738 --> 00:17:12.210
Come on, come on.

00:18:16.541 --> 00:18:17.747
Here.

00:18:18.317 --> 00:18:19.543
Start wiping down your finger prints.

00:18:19.578 --> 00:18:20.666
We don't want the cops
to know we were here.

00:18:20.701 --> 00:18:22.576
Go! Go! Come on!

00:18:26.878 --> 00:18:28.852
I'm gonna take a look inside.

00:18:34.855 --> 00:18:36.481
I'm telling you there
was nothing in there.

00:18:36.516 --> 00:18:38.818
There's no signs either.
Just like the Miller's house.

00:18:38.853 --> 00:18:41.873
I saw something in the
vision. Like a dark shape.

00:18:41.908 --> 00:18:43.077
Something was...

00:18:43.112 --> 00:18:44.831
Something was stalking Roger.

00:18:44.866 --> 00:18:47.665
Well, whatever it was I'm sure
it's not connected to their house.

00:18:47.700 --> 00:18:49.862
No, it's connected to the family itself.

00:18:49.897 --> 00:18:52.335
So, what do you think?
Like a ventral spirit?

00:18:52.370 --> 00:18:54.748
Oh, yeah. Few of them have been
known to ledge horn to families.

00:18:54.783 --> 00:18:56.356
They'll haunt them for years.

00:18:56.391 --> 00:18:59.142
Angier, Badges.

00:19:00.052 --> 00:19:01.522
Basically it was like a curse.

00:19:01.557 --> 00:19:04.158
Maybe Roger and Jim Miller got
involved in something heavy.

00:19:04.193 --> 00:19:07.337
Something curse worthy. And
now something's out for revenge.

00:19:07.372 --> 00:19:10.510
And they're making their family dying.

00:19:11.593 --> 00:19:14.345
Hey, you think Max is in danger?

00:19:14.380 --> 00:19:17.062
Let's figure out before he is.

00:19:17.097 --> 00:19:20.324
Well... I know one thing I have
in common with these people.

00:19:20.359 --> 00:19:22.046
What's that?

00:19:22.081 --> 00:19:24.463
Well, their families are cursed.

00:19:24.498 --> 00:19:26.446
Our family's not cursed.

00:19:26.481 --> 00:19:29.832
We're just had our dark spots.

00:19:30.942 --> 00:19:32.497
Our dark spots are...

00:19:32.532 --> 00:19:34.656
Pretty dark.

00:19:34.691 --> 00:19:36.780
You're dark.

00:19:40.204 --> 00:19:44.054
My mom's resting. She's
pretty packed. Of course.

00:19:44.416 --> 00:19:47.633
All these people kept
coming with like casseroles.

00:19:47.668 --> 00:19:50.219
I finally had to tell
them all to go away.

00:19:50.254 --> 00:19:54.723
You know, cause nothing says
I'm sorry like a tuna casserole.

00:20:07.015 --> 00:20:09.532
How are you holding up?

00:20:09.714 --> 00:20:11.377
I'm okay.

00:20:11.412 --> 00:20:14.796
Your dad and your uncle were close?

00:20:14.831 --> 00:20:17.621
Yeah, I guess. They were brothers.

00:20:17.656 --> 00:20:20.377
I use to hang out when I was little.

00:20:20.412 --> 00:20:24.653
But not lately, much?
No, it's not that. It's...

00:20:24.688 --> 00:20:27.099
We used to be neighbors
when I was a kid.

00:20:27.134 --> 00:20:29.476
We lived across town
in this house and...

00:20:29.511 --> 00:20:34.252
Uncle Roger lived next door so
he was over all the time. Right.

00:20:34.670 --> 00:20:39.526
So how was it in that
house when you were a kid?

00:20:39.561 --> 00:20:41.719
It was fine.

00:20:42.296 --> 00:20:43.641
Why?

00:20:43.676 --> 00:20:46.052
All good memories?

00:20:46.087 --> 00:20:48.851
You remember anything unusual?

00:20:48.886 --> 00:20:53.264
Something involving your
father and your uncle maybe?

00:20:54.451 --> 00:20:56.434
Why do you...?

00:20:56.608 --> 00:20:59.141
Why do you ask?

00:21:00.765 --> 00:21:03.212
It's just a question.

00:21:04.769 --> 00:21:09.061
No, there was nothing.
We were totally normal.

00:21:09.964 --> 00:21:12.933
Happy. Good.

00:21:13.803 --> 00:21:16.504
That's good.

00:21:17.145 --> 00:21:19.615
Well, you must be exhausted.

00:21:19.650 --> 00:21:22.086
We should take off. Right.

00:21:23.158 --> 00:21:26.565
Thanks. Yeah.

00:21:30.509 --> 00:21:32.860
Nobody's family is
totally normal and happy.

00:21:32.895 --> 00:21:35.212
You see when he was
talking about his old house?

00:21:35.247 --> 00:21:37.331
Sounded scared.

00:21:37.366 --> 00:21:39.268
Max isn't telling us everything.

00:21:39.303 --> 00:21:41.135
See we go find the old neighborhood?

00:21:41.170 --> 00:21:43.891
Find out what life it
was with the Millers.

00:21:48.333 --> 00:21:50.173
Have you lived in the
neighborhood very long?

00:21:50.208 --> 00:21:51.831
Yeah, almost twenty years now.

00:21:51.866 --> 00:21:53.049
It's nice and quiet.

00:21:53.084 --> 00:21:54.198
Why you looking to buy?

00:21:54.233 --> 00:21:56.248
No, no, actually we
were just wondering if...

00:21:56.283 --> 00:22:00.048
If you might recall a family that use to
live right across the street I believe.

00:22:00.083 --> 00:22:02.454
Yeah, the Millers. They
had a little boy named Max.

00:22:02.489 --> 00:22:04.177
Right.

00:22:04.700 --> 00:22:06.003
Yeah, I remember.

00:22:06.038 --> 00:22:08.971
Their brother had the place next door.

00:22:09.248 --> 00:22:11.409
So, what's this about?

00:22:11.444 --> 00:22:13.545
That poor kid okay?

00:22:13.580 --> 00:22:15.646
What do you mean?

00:22:16.008 --> 00:22:19.118
Well, in my life. I've never
seen a child treated like that.

00:22:19.153 --> 00:22:20.452
I mean, I'd hear Mr. Miller

00:22:20.487 --> 00:22:23.872
Yelling and throwing things clear
across the street. He was a...

00:22:23.907 --> 00:22:25.616
Mean drunk.

00:22:25.651 --> 00:22:27.541
Used to beat the tire out of Max.

00:22:27.576 --> 00:22:31.329
Bruises. Broke his arm
two times that I know of.

00:22:31.364 --> 00:22:33.811
And this was going on regularly?

00:22:33.846 --> 00:22:35.607
Practically everyday.

00:22:35.642 --> 00:22:37.404
In fact that thug brother of his

00:22:37.439 --> 00:22:40.928
Was just as likely take a swing
at the boy. But the worst part...

00:22:40.963 --> 00:22:42.868
Was his step mother.

00:22:42.903 --> 00:22:45.085
She just...

00:22:45.120 --> 00:22:48.466
Stand there, checked out. Never
lifted a finger to protect him.

00:22:48.501 --> 00:22:51.082
I must have called the
police seven or eight times.

00:22:51.117 --> 00:22:53.664
Never did any good. Now,
you said 'step mother'.

00:22:53.699 --> 00:22:56.723
I think his real mom
died. Some sort of...

00:22:56.758 --> 00:22:59.647
Accident. Car accident I think.

00:22:59.682 --> 00:23:01.848
Are you okay there?

00:23:03.631 --> 00:23:05.832
Uh, yeah. Thanks for your time.

00:23:05.867 --> 00:23:08.034
Oh, yeah. Thank you. Let's go.

00:23:09.096 --> 00:23:10.803
Oh, god.

00:23:22.419 --> 00:23:25.045
I don't know what you mean by that.

00:23:25.080 --> 00:23:28.319
You know I didn't do
anything. That's right.

00:23:28.354 --> 00:23:31.857
You didn't do anything.

00:23:32.560 --> 00:23:36.219
You didn't stop them. Not once.

00:23:36.748 --> 00:23:38.763
How did you...?

00:23:41.498 --> 00:23:44.106
Max! Please!

00:23:56.085 --> 00:24:01.077
But every time you
stood there and watched.

00:24:01.112 --> 00:24:04.379
Pretending it wasn't happening.

00:24:04.414 --> 00:24:07.646
I'm sorry. No, you're not.

00:24:08.126 --> 00:24:11.180
You just don't want to die.

00:24:24.010 --> 00:24:25.880
Max is doing it.

00:24:25.915 --> 00:24:28.013
Everything I've been seeing.

00:24:28.048 --> 00:24:31.037
Are you sure about
this? Yeah, I saw him.

00:24:31.212 --> 00:24:32.630
How is he pulling it off?

00:24:32.665 --> 00:24:34.591
I don't know. Looks like telekinesis.

00:24:34.626 --> 00:24:36.482
So, he's Psychic? He's a spoon bender?

00:24:36.517 --> 00:24:39.146
I didn't even realize but
this whole time he was there.

00:24:39.181 --> 00:24:41.521
He was outside of the
garage when his dad died.

00:24:41.556 --> 00:24:43.862
He was in the apartment
when his uncle died.

00:24:43.897 --> 00:24:45.354
His visions this whole time.

00:24:45.389 --> 00:24:49.099
I wasn't connected to the
Millers. I was connecting to Max.

00:24:49.276 --> 00:24:52.054
The thing I don't know
is why man. I guess...

00:24:52.089 --> 00:24:53.902
Cause we are so alike?

00:24:53.937 --> 00:24:56.748
What are you talking about?
Dude's nothing like you.

00:24:56.783 --> 00:24:59.172
Oh, we both have psychic abilities.

00:24:59.207 --> 00:25:00.817
We're both... Both what?

00:25:00.852 --> 00:25:02.392
Sam, Max is a monster.

00:25:02.427 --> 00:25:04.386
He's already killed two people
now he's going for a third.

00:25:04.421 --> 00:25:07.107
With all he went through. The beatings.

00:25:07.142 --> 00:25:08.502
To want revenge on those people.

00:25:08.537 --> 00:25:11.163
I'm sorry man, I hate to
say it. It's not that insane.

00:25:11.198 --> 00:25:13.687
Yeah, but it doesn't justify
murdering your entire family.

00:25:13.722 --> 00:25:16.176
Dean... He's no different than
anything else we've hunted.

00:25:16.211 --> 00:25:18.124
All right, we've got to end it.

00:25:19.155 --> 00:25:21.271
We're not gonna kill Max.

00:25:21.306 --> 00:25:22.527
Then what?

00:25:22.562 --> 00:25:24.794
I hand him over to the cops
and say Lock him up, officer.

00:25:24.829 --> 00:25:27.227
He kills with his power
of his mind. Forget it.

00:25:27.262 --> 00:25:29.877
No way man. Sam! Do...

00:25:29.912 --> 00:25:31.673
He's a person.

00:25:31.708 --> 00:25:33.021
We can talk to him.

00:25:33.056 --> 00:25:36.773
Hey! Promise me you'll
follow my lead on this one.

00:25:37.663 --> 00:25:39.285
All right, fine.

00:25:39.320 --> 00:25:41.694
But I'm not letting
him hurt anyone else.

00:25:52.380 --> 00:25:56.338
You know I never did
anything. That's right.

00:25:56.373 --> 00:25:59.405
You didn't do anything.

00:25:59.682 --> 00:26:02.895
You didn't stop them. Not once.

00:26:03.991 --> 00:26:05.869
Fathers?

00:26:07.996 --> 00:26:11.332
What are you doing here? Oh...

00:26:11.367 --> 00:26:13.120
Sorry to interrupt.

00:26:13.155 --> 00:26:14.839
Max, could we uh...

00:26:14.874 --> 00:26:19.013
Could we talk to you
outside for just one second?

00:26:20.160 --> 00:26:22.287
About what?

00:26:22.322 --> 00:26:24.205
It's... It's private.

00:26:24.240 --> 00:26:27.016
Um... I wouldn't want to
bother your mother with it.

00:26:27.051 --> 00:26:30.026
We won't be long at
all though. I promise.

00:26:36.087 --> 00:26:37.528
Okay.

00:26:37.563 --> 00:26:38.969
Great.

00:27:05.117 --> 00:27:07.146
You're not priests!

00:27:13.245 --> 00:27:14.555
Max! What's happening?

00:27:14.590 --> 00:27:16.896
Shut up! What are you doing?

00:27:19.553 --> 00:27:21.843
I said shut up! Max, calm down.

00:27:21.878 --> 00:27:23.786
Who are you? We just
want to talk to you.

00:27:23.821 --> 00:27:25.695
Yeah, right. That's
why you brought this.

00:27:25.730 --> 00:27:27.389
That was a mistake, all right?

00:27:27.424 --> 00:27:29.651
So was lying about who we
were. But no more lying Max.

00:27:29.686 --> 00:27:31.480
Okay? Just please.

00:27:31.515 --> 00:27:34.762
Just hear me out. About what?

00:27:35.203 --> 00:27:37.847
I saw you do it.

00:27:37.882 --> 00:27:41.993
I saw you kill your dad and
your uncle before it happened.

00:27:42.028 --> 00:27:45.658
What? I'm having visions about you.

00:27:45.693 --> 00:27:47.550
You're crazy.

00:27:47.585 --> 00:27:49.842
So, you weren't gonna launch
a knife at your step mom?

00:27:49.877 --> 00:27:51.171
Right here?

00:27:51.206 --> 00:27:53.719
Isn't that hard to believe?
Max, look what you can do?

00:27:53.754 --> 00:27:56.630
Max, I was drawn here, all right?

00:27:57.207 --> 00:28:00.071
I think I'm here to help you.

00:28:02.943 --> 00:28:05.523
No one can help me.

00:28:05.558 --> 00:28:06.883
Let me try.

00:28:06.918 --> 00:28:08.330
We'll just talk.

00:28:08.365 --> 00:28:09.674
Me and you.

00:28:09.709 --> 00:28:13.938
We'll get Dean and Alice
out of here. No, no way.

00:28:14.651 --> 00:28:16.765
Nobody leaves this house!

00:28:16.800 --> 00:28:19.251
And nobody has to, all
right? They'll just...

00:28:19.286 --> 00:28:20.528
They'll just go upstairs.

00:28:20.563 --> 00:28:22.313
Sam, I'm not leaving you alone with him.

00:28:22.348 --> 00:28:23.961
Yes, you are.

00:28:23.996 --> 00:28:25.540
Look, Max...

00:28:25.575 --> 00:28:27.818
You're in charge here. All
right? We all know that.

00:28:27.853 --> 00:28:30.061
No one's gonna do anything
that you don't want to do.

00:28:30.096 --> 00:28:33.625
But I'm talking five
minutes here man. Sam...

00:28:36.242 --> 00:28:38.475
Five minutes?

00:28:39.553 --> 00:28:40.961
Go.

00:28:53.780 --> 00:28:55.147
Come on.

00:28:59.776 --> 00:29:01.199
Look.

00:29:01.234 --> 00:29:03.800
I can't begin to understand
what you went through.

00:29:03.835 --> 00:29:06.442
That's right, you can't. Max...

00:29:06.477 --> 00:29:08.960
This has to stop. It will.

00:29:08.995 --> 00:29:11.443
After my step mother... No.

00:29:11.478 --> 00:29:13.428
You need to let her go.

00:29:13.463 --> 00:29:15.235
Why?

00:29:16.189 --> 00:29:18.143
Did she beat you?

00:29:18.178 --> 00:29:19.493
No.

00:29:19.528 --> 00:29:24.126
But she never tried to save
me. She's part of it too.

00:29:25.356 --> 00:29:27.087
Look what they did to you.

00:29:27.122 --> 00:29:31.016
Look what they all
did to you growing up.

00:29:31.051 --> 00:29:34.911
They deserve to be punished. Growing up?

00:29:34.946 --> 00:29:37.806
Try last week.

00:29:43.295 --> 00:29:45.312
My dad still hits me.

00:29:45.347 --> 00:29:48.847
Just in places people wouldn't see it.

00:29:49.848 --> 00:29:52.994
Old habits die hard I guess.

00:29:56.720 --> 00:29:58.654
I'm sorry.

00:30:04.118 --> 00:30:08.017
When I first found out
I could move things.

00:30:08.052 --> 00:30:10.356
It was a gift.

00:30:10.840 --> 00:30:14.560
My whole life I was helpless.

00:30:14.595 --> 00:30:17.163
But now I have this.

00:30:18.030 --> 00:30:20.333
So, last week...

00:30:20.368 --> 00:30:22.602
Dad gets drunk.

00:30:22.637 --> 00:30:25.085
First time in a long time.

00:30:25.120 --> 00:30:27.498
And he beats me to hell.

00:30:27.533 --> 00:30:30.274
It's the first time in a long time.

00:30:30.510 --> 00:30:33.225
And I do what I had to do.

00:30:33.260 --> 00:30:36.016
Why didn't you just leave?

00:30:36.051 --> 00:30:38.772
It isn't about getting away.

00:30:39.744 --> 00:30:43.868
Just knowing that they'd
still be out there.

00:30:44.151 --> 00:30:49.248
It was about not being afraid.

00:30:50.953 --> 00:30:53.736
When my dad used to look at me.

00:30:53.771 --> 00:30:56.484
There was hate in his eyes.

00:30:56.519 --> 00:31:00.061
Do you know what that feels like?

00:31:02.218 --> 00:31:03.481
No.

00:31:03.516 --> 00:31:06.609
He blamed me for everything.

00:31:06.644 --> 00:31:09.703
For his job. For his life.

00:31:09.738 --> 00:31:12.529
For my mom's death.

00:31:12.564 --> 00:31:15.876
Why did he blame you
for your mom's death?

00:31:18.498 --> 00:31:21.215
Because she died in my nursery.

00:31:21.250 --> 00:31:24.565
While I was asleep in my crib.

00:31:24.600 --> 00:31:27.881
As if that makes it my fault.

00:31:28.097 --> 00:31:30.145
She died in your nursery?

00:31:30.180 --> 00:31:31.389
Yeah.

00:31:31.424 --> 00:31:34.502
There was a fire and he get drunk

00:31:34.537 --> 00:31:38.602
And blab along like she
died in some insane way.

00:31:38.637 --> 00:31:41.029
He said that she burned up.

00:31:41.064 --> 00:31:43.895
Pinned to the ceiling.

00:31:49.017 --> 00:31:51.139
Listen to me Max.

00:31:51.609 --> 00:31:53.265
What your dad said.

00:31:53.300 --> 00:31:56.004
About what happened to your mom.

00:31:56.951 --> 00:31:59.203
It's real.

00:32:00.357 --> 00:32:02.053
What?

00:32:02.088 --> 00:32:04.105
It happened to my mom too.

00:32:04.140 --> 00:32:06.061
Exactly the same.

00:32:06.096 --> 00:32:07.947
My nursery, my crib.

00:32:07.982 --> 00:32:10.753
My dad saw her in the ceiling.

00:32:11.294 --> 00:32:14.674
Your dad must have been
as drunk as mine. No.

00:32:14.709 --> 00:32:16.571
No, it's the same thing, Max.

00:32:16.606 --> 00:32:18.831
The same thing killed our mothers.

00:32:18.866 --> 00:32:21.176
That's impossible.

00:32:21.525 --> 00:32:25.117
This must be why I've been
having visions during the day.

00:32:25.291 --> 00:32:27.674
Why they're getting more intense.

00:32:27.866 --> 00:32:31.308
Cause you and I must be
connected in some way.

00:32:31.490 --> 00:32:34.346
Your abilities started six,
seven months ago, right?

00:32:34.381 --> 00:32:36.193
Out of the blue?

00:32:36.469 --> 00:32:37.544
How'd you know that?

00:32:37.579 --> 00:32:39.603
Because that's when my
abilities started Max.

00:32:39.638 --> 00:32:42.218
I mean, yours seem to be much
further along but still this...

00:32:42.253 --> 00:32:44.444
This means something. Right?

00:32:44.479 --> 00:32:49.404
I mean, for some reason.
You and I were chosen.

00:32:51.119 --> 00:32:53.290
For what?

00:32:54.154 --> 00:32:56.162
I don't know.

00:32:56.909 --> 00:32:59.114
But Dean and I... My brother and I...

00:32:59.149 --> 00:33:01.320
We're hunting for your mom's killer.

00:33:01.355 --> 00:33:03.003
We can find answers.

00:33:03.038 --> 00:33:05.614
Answers that can answer us both.

00:33:05.649 --> 00:33:08.191
But you got to let us go Max.

00:33:08.533 --> 00:33:11.826
You got to let your step mother go.

00:33:24.693 --> 00:33:26.637
No.

00:33:27.140 --> 00:33:29.987
What they did to me.

00:33:30.022 --> 00:33:32.799
I still have nightmares.

00:33:32.834 --> 00:33:35.563
I'm still scared all the time. Like...

00:33:35.598 --> 00:33:38.042
I'm waiting for that next beating.

00:33:38.077 --> 00:33:42.076
I'm just tired of being scared.
If I do this, it'll be all over.

00:33:42.111 --> 00:33:43.689
No, don't you get it?

00:33:43.724 --> 00:33:44.807
It won't.

00:33:44.842 --> 00:33:46.614
The nightmares won't end Max.

00:33:46.649 --> 00:33:48.459
Not like this.

00:33:48.494 --> 00:33:50.270
There's just...

00:33:50.431 --> 00:33:52.400
More pain.

00:33:52.643 --> 00:33:55.276
And it makes you as bad as them.

00:33:56.075 --> 00:33:58.155
Max...

00:33:58.742 --> 00:34:02.326
You don't have to go
this all by yourself.

00:34:07.241 --> 00:34:09.409
I'm sorry.

00:34:10.119 --> 00:34:11.564
No!

00:34:12.346 --> 00:34:13.946
Max!

00:34:15.777 --> 00:34:17.222
No!

00:34:17.257 --> 00:34:18.667
Max!

00:34:43.511 --> 00:34:44.873
Max!

00:34:47.088 --> 00:34:48.679
Son of a...

00:34:50.403 --> 00:34:51.775
Max.

00:34:52.380 --> 00:34:53.949
Max.

00:34:57.208 --> 00:34:58.743
No.

00:35:07.472 --> 00:35:09.067
Max.

00:35:10.587 --> 00:35:12.724
Stay back.

00:35:13.084 --> 00:35:14.918
It's not about you.

00:35:14.953 --> 00:35:18.012
If you want to kill. You got
to go through with me first.

00:35:19.349 --> 00:35:20.996
Okay.

00:35:39.394 --> 00:35:40.683
No!

00:35:41.415 --> 00:35:42.998
No!

00:35:54.655 --> 00:35:56.522
Max...

00:35:57.421 --> 00:35:59.132
No.

00:35:59.518 --> 00:36:01.634
Stay back.

00:36:01.832 --> 00:36:03.534
It's not about you.

00:36:03.569 --> 00:36:07.064
If you want to kill. You got
to go through with me first.

00:36:07.873 --> 00:36:09.741
Okay.

00:36:11.442 --> 00:36:13.973
No, don't! Don't!

00:36:14.008 --> 00:36:16.505
Please! Please Max!

00:36:17.607 --> 00:36:19.137
Max...

00:36:19.172 --> 00:36:21.551
We can help you.

00:36:21.764 --> 00:36:24.715
But this... What you're doing...

00:36:24.936 --> 00:36:27.052
It's not the solution.

00:36:27.087 --> 00:36:30.400
It's not gonna fix anything.

00:36:40.477 --> 00:36:43.009
You're right.

00:36:45.667 --> 00:36:47.192
No!

00:36:57.597 --> 00:36:59.819
Max attacked me.

00:36:59.854 --> 00:37:02.627
He threatened me with a gun.

00:37:03.330 --> 00:37:05.261
And these two?

00:37:07.214 --> 00:37:09.272
They're...

00:37:09.307 --> 00:37:11.731
Family friends.

00:37:12.779 --> 00:37:17.380
I called them as soon as
Max arrived. I was scared.

00:37:17.570 --> 00:37:20.088
They tried to stop him.

00:37:20.123 --> 00:37:22.607
They fought for the gun.

00:37:22.807 --> 00:37:25.669
Where did Max hid the gun?

00:37:27.511 --> 00:37:30.863
I don't know. He...

00:37:30.898 --> 00:37:34.215
Showed up and he...

00:37:37.653 --> 00:37:39.955
It's all right, Mrs. Miller.

00:37:41.405 --> 00:37:44.698
I lost everyone.

00:37:45.803 --> 00:37:47.403
Okay.

00:37:47.739 --> 00:37:49.826
We'll give you a call if we
have any further questions.

00:37:49.861 --> 00:37:51.624
Thanks officer.

00:37:52.076 --> 00:37:53.499
Come on.

00:38:06.167 --> 00:38:08.906
Freggis said something else.

00:38:08.941 --> 00:38:11.578
Got him through it
somehow. Don't do that.

00:38:11.613 --> 00:38:13.811
Do what? Told you yourself.

00:38:13.846 --> 00:38:16.689
It wouldn't matter what you
said. Max was too far gone.

00:38:16.724 --> 00:38:19.532
When I think about how he
looked at me man right before...

00:38:19.726 --> 00:38:21.064
I should have done something.

00:38:21.099 --> 00:38:23.283
Come on, man. You risked your life.

00:38:23.318 --> 00:38:26.725
I mean, yeah. If we gotten
there twenty years earlier...

00:38:28.626 --> 00:38:30.380
Well, I'll tell you one thing.

00:38:30.415 --> 00:38:32.551
We're lucky we had dad.

00:38:35.171 --> 00:38:38.728
I never thought you say that.

00:38:38.931 --> 00:38:40.205
Well...

00:38:40.240 --> 00:38:42.862
He could have gone away more after mom.

00:38:42.897 --> 00:38:48.393
A little more tequila a
little less demon hunting.

00:38:48.428 --> 00:38:51.860
Then we would have Max's childhood.

00:38:52.945 --> 00:38:55.355
All things considered.

00:38:55.390 --> 00:38:57.766
We turned out okay.

00:38:57.801 --> 00:39:00.116
Thanks to him.

00:39:03.817 --> 00:39:06.016
All things considered.

00:39:15.155 --> 00:39:16.411
Dean, I've been thinking.

00:39:16.446 --> 00:39:17.632
That's never a good thing.

00:39:17.667 --> 00:39:20.584
I'm serious. I've been thinking...

00:39:20.619 --> 00:39:24.328
Why would this demon or
whatever it is. Why would it...

00:39:24.363 --> 00:39:26.786
Kill mom and Jessica and Max's mother?

00:39:26.821 --> 00:39:28.409
You know, what does it want?

00:39:28.444 --> 00:39:30.643
No idea. Well, you think maybe...

00:39:30.678 --> 00:39:33.615
It was after us? After...

00:39:33.650 --> 00:39:36.457
Max and me? Why would you think that?

00:39:36.690 --> 00:39:37.964
I mean...

00:39:37.999 --> 00:39:39.962
Either telekinesis are premonitions.

00:39:39.997 --> 00:39:41.891
We both had abilities, you know.

00:39:41.926 --> 00:39:44.063
Maybe it was after us for some reason.

00:39:44.098 --> 00:39:47.212
Sam, if it wanted you. It
would have just taken you.

00:39:47.247 --> 00:39:48.398
Okay?

00:39:48.433 --> 00:39:50.010
This is not your fault.

00:39:50.045 --> 00:39:51.829
It is not about you.

00:39:51.864 --> 00:39:53.613
Then what is it about?

00:39:53.812 --> 00:39:56.289
It's about that damn thing
that did this to our family.

00:39:56.324 --> 00:39:59.072
That thing that we're gonna
find that thing we're gonna kill.

00:39:59.107 --> 00:40:01.218
And that's all.

00:40:02.497 --> 00:40:04.920
Actually, there's a...

00:40:04.955 --> 00:40:07.343
Something else too.

00:40:07.969 --> 00:40:09.346
Oh, geez what?

00:40:09.381 --> 00:40:12.584
When Max locked me in that closet.

00:40:12.619 --> 00:40:15.787
That big cabinet against the door.

00:40:16.139 --> 00:40:18.138
I moved it.

00:40:19.157 --> 00:40:22.016
Yeah, you're a little more up the body
strength than I gave you credit for.

00:40:22.051 --> 00:40:25.028
No man. I moved it. Like...

00:40:25.063 --> 00:40:27.164
Max.

00:40:29.908 --> 00:40:31.717
Oh.

00:40:33.636 --> 00:40:35.590
Right.

00:40:35.625 --> 00:40:37.544
Yeah.

00:40:44.233 --> 00:40:46.401
Bend this.

00:40:46.640 --> 00:40:48.312
I can't turn it on and off Dean.

00:40:48.347 --> 00:40:49.775
Then how'd you do it? I don't know.

00:40:49.810 --> 00:40:51.939
I can't control it. I just...

00:40:51.974 --> 00:40:55.511
I saw you die and it just came
out of me like a... Like a punch.

00:40:55.546 --> 00:40:56.827
You know, like a...

00:40:56.862 --> 00:40:59.633
Like a freak adrenaline thing.

00:41:03.276 --> 00:41:05.778
Well, I'm sure it won't happen again.

00:41:07.534 --> 00:41:09.266
Yeah, maybe.

00:41:09.301 --> 00:41:10.430
Aren't you worried man?

00:41:10.465 --> 00:41:13.143
Aren't you worried that I can
turn into Max or something?

00:41:13.178 --> 00:41:15.889
Nope. No way.

00:41:16.078 --> 00:41:17.273
You know why?

00:41:17.308 --> 00:41:18.959
No, why?

00:41:18.994 --> 00:41:21.230
Cause you got one advantage
that Max didn't have.

00:41:21.265 --> 00:41:22.983
Dad?

00:41:23.154 --> 00:41:25.392
Because dad's not here, Dean.

00:41:25.427 --> 00:41:27.070
No.

00:41:27.666 --> 00:41:29.748
Me.

00:41:30.897 --> 00:41:32.591
As long as I'm around...

00:41:32.626 --> 00:41:35.384
Nothing bad is gonna happen to you.

00:41:36.956 --> 00:41:38.653
Now then.

00:41:38.688 --> 00:41:41.526
I know what we need to
do with your premonitions.

00:41:41.561 --> 00:41:43.549
I know where we've got to go.

00:41:43.584 --> 00:41:45.599
Where?

00:41:45.830 --> 00:41:47.924
Vegas.

00:41:51.769 --> 00:41:54.088
What? Come on man.

00:41:54.285 --> 00:41:57.411
Craps table. We'd clean up.



00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:07.000
